    <h2>Honourable Mentions</h2>

    <p><strong>Skruf Super White</strong> — Swedish manufacturing, white pouch, tobacco-free. Premium quality at a step below Kelly White. Excellent for users who want Scandinavian pedigree without the highest premium.</p>

    <p><strong>FUMI</strong> — Turkish brand, 30 mg strength, strong competitor to Siberia. Slightly smoother flavour, fractionally cheaper. Fewer retailers stock it, but worth seeking out if extreme strength is your goal.</p>

    <p><strong>ACE</strong> — Scandinavian heritage, white pouches, subtle spice notes. Less widely available than ZYN or VELO, but loyal users swear by the flavour refinement.</p>

    <p><strong>XQS</strong> — Budget-friendly, wide strength range (1–18 mg), good all-rounder. Not a category winner, but solid if your local shop stocks it and price matters most.</p>

    <h2>How to Find Your Perfect Pouch</h2>

    <p><strong>Step 1: Choose Your Strength</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Beginner (first-time ever):</strong> 3–4 mg (VELO Simply Spearmint Mini)</li>
      <li><strong>Light daily use:</strong> 6–8 mg (ZYN Cool Mint Regular, LOOP Mint Mania)</li>
      <li><strong>Regular daily use:</strong> 10–13.5 mg (ZYN Menthol Ice Slim, VELO medium range)</li>
      <li><strong>Heavy daily use:</strong> 18+ mg (Siberia, FUMI, ZYN Slim S5)</li>
    </ul>

    <p><strong>Step 2: Pick Your Flavour Profile</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Mint lovers → ZYN Menthol Ice</li>
      <li>Flavour explorers → VELO range</li>
      <li>Traditionalists → Kelly White, Skruf</li>
      <li>Minimalists → ZYN Cool Mint</li>
    </ul>

    <p><strong>Step 3: Consider Format</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Regular:</strong> Larger pouch, more saliva, longer release (90 mins+). Good for all-day sessions.</li>
      <li><strong>Slim:</strong> Smaller pouch, discreet, faster release (45–60 mins). Ideal for work or social settings.</li>
      <li><strong>Mini:</strong> Smallest format, fastest release. Perfect for new users and precise control.</li>
    </ul>

    <p><strong>Step 4: Start with One Tin</strong></p>
    <p>Never bulk-buy. Your preference will shift as you find your rhythm. Buy a single tin, use for a week, then decide if you want more or prefer to switch.</p>

    <p>If you're stuck, <a href="/flavor-quiz">take our flavour quiz</a> — 30 seconds of questions, personalised recommendations.</p>

    <h2>FAQ: Your Top Nicotine Pouch Questions Answered</h2>

    <h3>What strength nicotine pouch should I start with?</h3>
    <p>If you're new to nicotine pouches, start with 3–6 mg/pouch. This delivers a light buzz without overwhelming effects. VELO Simply Spearmint Mini at 4 mg is specifically designed for beginners — the small format makes it easy to control duration and intensity.</p>

    <h3>Are stronger nicotine pouches safer than smoking?</h3>
    <p>Nicotine pouches are fundamentally different from smoking because they don't involve combustion. Even high-strength pouches like Siberia (33 mg/g) pose no smoke-related risks. However, very high strength is habit-forming and not recommended for casual users. Start with moderate strength and increase only if you're a regular user.</p>

    <h3>How long does a nicotine pouch last?</h3>
    <p>Most nicotine pouches release their nicotine over 30–60 minutes. Slim formats tend to last slightly shorter. You can control duration by removing the pouch early. For all-day use, one pouch every 1–2 hours is typical among regular users.</p>

    <h3>What's the difference between ZYN and VELO?</h3>
    <p>ZYN is the simpler all-round pick with a more standardized lineup, while VELO offers more flavour experimentation and a broader live assortment on SnusFriend. Both are high-quality; the choice comes down to whether you prefer consistency (ZYN) or a wider menu of formats and flavours (VELO).</p>

    <h3>Can I use nicotine pouches if I'm pregnant?</h3>
    <p>Nicotine is harmful to foetal development. You should not use any nicotine product — pouches, cigarettes, or vaping — during pregnancy. If you're trying to quit nicotine, speak with a healthcare provider about evidence-based cessation support.</p>

    <h2>The Bottom Line</h2>

    <p>The nicotine pouch market is crowded, but quality is increasingly concentrated in a handful of proven leaders. If you want consistency and availability, ZYN Cool Mint wins. If you're exploring, VELO's breadth is unmatched. If you want refined quality, Kelly White and Skruf deliver.</p>
    <p>Based on our analysis of over {facts.productCountLabel} products across {facts.brandCountLabel} brands, the safest conclusion is that a small group of mainstream and Scandinavian brands now carries most of the serious buying consideration. Exact market-share movements vary too much by country to present as a timeless fact here.</p>

    <p>The "best" pouch is the one you reach for daily. Use our category winners as a starting point, commit to a tin, and adjust from there. Most users settle into one or two trusted brands within weeks.</p>

